 "blurb": "The picture breaks into real 3D pieces that are knocked loose from an impact point and fall under gravity, colliding with each other and tumbling in true 3D before dropping out of frame or settling on a floor, uncovering whatever is behind. The collision is a native physics bake that re-runs the instant you change a setting, so it stays fast; a seed makes it random yet repeatable. Type a range such as (4, 14) into Gravity, Force, Spin, Spread or Piece weight and every piece picks its own value from it; click a piece on the Program monitor to give that one piece its own weight and gravity. Drag the impact on the Program monitor and key Progress, or set it to fire on the clip's out point.",
